DESCRIPTION:Family Health History Day is one of the rare observances on thi
 s calendar with a documented founder\, a documented date and a stated purp
 ose. In November 2004 the U.S. Surgeon General\, Richard H. Carmona\, decl
 ared Thanksgiving Day the first annual National Family History Day\, on th
 e reasoning that the one day a year when an extended family is in the same
  room is the day to ask relatives what they have been diagnosed with and w
 hat their parents died of. Because it is pinned to Thanksgiving rather tha
 n to a fixed date\, it moves: in 2026 it falls on November 26.\n\nhttps://
 todaycelebrates.com/holiday/family-health-history-day/
